        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A portable power station can run an air conditioner if its inverter survives the compressor's startup surge, and the best fit is a small 5,000 to 6,000 BTU window unit on a 2,000Wh or larger station. Expect a few hours of cooling from a single battery, more if the compressor cycles and the room is well sealed, and far less from portable ACs and larger window units.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            To make it genuinely useful, choose an inverter AC, pre-cool on grid power, raise the thermostat a few degrees and add solar so the hottest hours run on sunshine. If you need a whole house cooled or a big AC run all night, the battery you would need costs more than the alternatives, and a generator or whole-home system is the more honest answer.
          </p>
        </div>

